{
  "sn12.12:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.12 ",
  "sn12.12:0.2": "2. Fuel ",
  "sn12.12:0.3": "Phagguna of the Top-Knot ",
  "sn12.12:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.12:1.2": "“Mendicants, these four fuels maintain sentient beings that have been born and help those about to be born. ",
  "sn12.12:1.3": "What four? ",
  "sn12.12:1.4": "Edible food, whether solid or subtle; contact is the second, mental intention the third, and consciousness the fourth. ",
  "sn12.12:1.5": "These are the four fuels that maintain sentient beings that have been born and help those that are about to be born.” ",
  "sn12.12:2.1": "When he said this, Venerable Phagguna of the Top-Knot said to the Buddha, ",
  "sn12.12:2.2": "“But sir, who consumes consciousness as fuel?” ",
  "sn12.12:2.3": "“That’s not a cogent question,” said the Buddha. ",
  "sn12.12:2.4": "“I don’t speak of one who consumes. ",
  "sn12.12:2.5": "If I were to speak of one who consumes, then it would be cogent to ask ",
  "sn12.12:2.6": "who consumes. ",
  "sn12.12:2.7": "But I don’t speak like that. ",
  "sn12.12:2.8": "Hence it would be cogent to ask: ",
  "sn12.12:2.9": "‘For what is consciousness the fuel?’ ",
  "sn12.12:2.10": "And a cogent answer to this would be: ",
  "sn12.12:2.11": "‘Consciousness as fuel is a requirement for regeneration into a new state of existence in the future. When the being is present, there are the six sense fields. The six sense fields are requirements for contact.’” ",
